Explain how you would define a user-centered checkout SLI.|A dashboard tracks CPU but users report failed checkouts. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would negotiate a realistic SLO.|Teams argue over whether current reliability is sufficient. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how an error-budget policy changes engineering priorities.|A service exhausts its error budget during repeated risky releases. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would organize the first minutes of a major incident.|Several responders make conflicting production changes. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain when rollback is a better first step than live debugging.|A recent release is strongly correlated with failures and rollback is safe. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how a postmortem should change the system.|The same outage recurs after a report with vague recommendations. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would identify and reduce a source of toil.|Engineers manually perform the same routine provisioning each day. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would test and maintain an operational runbook.|A responder follows an old procedure and worsens an outage. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain short and long windows in error-budget alerting.|A brief spike triggers pages despite negligible long-term budget impact. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would measure tail latency without losing user context.|Mean latency is stable but a subset of users sees long delays. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would reduce alert fatigue without hiding real failures.|Responders receive hundreds of nonactionable overnight alerts. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain capacity planning for a service that must tolerate one zone failure.|One zone fails and surviving instances immediately saturate. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain a load-shedding policy and how clients should react.|A backend is overloaded and queues grow without bound. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would propagate backpressure through a pipeline.|A queue grows faster than workers can drain it. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would prevent retry amplification across services.|Three service layers each retry failed calls several times. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain a practical restore test and its acceptance criteria.|Backups succeed but no one has restored the current application version. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would validate an end-to-end RTO.|A recovery plan promises one hour but identity recovery takes two hours. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain RPO and how you would measure whether it is achievable.|A restore loses six hours of writes despite a one-hour RPO. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain canary evaluation and automatic rollback criteria.|A new version raises error rates only for one request category. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain feature-flag rollback limits and cleanup responsibilities.|A newly enabled feature causes a dependency overload. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how dependency mapping changes incident diagnosis.|Several services fail after a shared identity system outage. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how to distinguish optional from critical dependencies.|Recommendations fail but checkout can work without them. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would design a small resilience experiment.|A team proposes an unbounded production failure test. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain what belongs in a useful incident status update.|Support receives conflicting guesses from different responders. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would prevent reliability metrics from masking small cohorts.|One region is down but global availability remains above target. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would prevent a thundering herd during recovery.|A restored service is overwhelmed by reconnecting clients. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how business invariants guide partition-time behavior.|A partition forces a decision for account-balance updates. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would choose between two reliability improvement projects.|A rare failure affects all customers while frequent minor alerts affect none. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain pitfalls in measuring incident response performance.|A dashboard improves after severe incidents are reclassified away. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
Explain how you would design and validate automated remediation.|An automated restart loop repeatedly disrupts healthy instances. Which observations would distinguish the likely causes, and how would you verify recovery?
